BND-09: round TotalDuration to the nearest second instead of truncating it

TotalDuration was floor((EndDate - StartDate)*86400 + (EndTime - StartTime)*86400).
The times are day fractions (s/86400), so the product is often one ulp below
the whole number of seconds (3779.9999999999995 for 01:03) and floor() drops
a second: the run stops at END - 1 s and the last reporting period is never
saved. Add 0.5 before the floor, in project_validate() and in the two API
setters (swmm_STARTDATE, swmm_ENDDATE) that repeat the formula.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-09_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/project.c b/src/legacy/engine/project.c
index d24c17f..383de4b 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/project.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/project.c
@@ -170,7 +170,8 @@ void project_readInput()
     else
     {
         // --- compute total duration of simulation in seconds
-        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY);
+        //     (rounded, since the day fractions rarely multiply out exactly)
+        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY + 0.5);
 
         // --- reporting step must be <= total duration
         if ( (double)ReportStep > TotalDuration )
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
index 4096c9a..c6f543c 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
@@ -3239,7 +3239,7 @@ static int setSystemValue(int property, double value)
         datetime_decodeTime(value, &h, &mm, &s);
         StartDate = datetime_encodeDate(y, m, d);
         StartTime = datetime_encodeTime(h, mm, s);
-        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY);
+        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY + 0.5);
         // convert total duration to milliseconds
         TotalDuration *= 1000.0;
         return 0;
@@ -3267,7 +3267,7 @@ static int setSystemValue(int property, double value)
         datetime_decodeTime(value, &h, &mm, &s);
         EndDate = datetime_encodeDate(y, m, d);
         EndTime = datetime_encodeTime(h, mm, s);
-        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY);
+        TotalDuration = floor((EndDate - StartDate) * SECperDAY + (EndTime - StartTime) * SECperDAY + 0.5);
         // convert total duration to milliseconds
         TotalDuration *= 1000.0;
         return 0;
